A view messaged after its superview let go of it, and two selectors that were not here.

THE CURRENCY MANAGER OPENS. Money Manager EX crashed every time its New Database Wizard tried to
build that panel; it now shows its currency list, Online Update, Show All, Search, Select and Close,
LOOKED AT. Three defects were between here and there and the first one is ours outright.

ONE, A USE AFTER FREE THAT THIS PORT INTRODUCED. removeFromSuperview ends with

    [removeFrom _removeViewWithoutDisplay: self];   removeObjectIdenticalTo:, usually the last ref
    [window _invalidateTrackingAreas];
    [self _ciderUpdateAppearanceTree];              ours, added so a controller hears it went away

so the view could be deallocated by the removal and then messaged. The core named it exactly:
objc_msgSend+29, and the selector register read out of the AppKit image at that address gives
_ciderUpdateAppearanceTree. A retain across the tail and a release at the end, which is the point
where dying is safe. Not autorelease, so it does not depend on a pool being in place.

TWO, NSCell controlTint and setControlTint:. Stored and answered, which is all the tint ever was
here: every control draws from the colour table rather than from it. It has to EXIST because an
unrecognized selector in a wxWidgets application becomes Unhandled unknown exception and terminates
the process. Money Manager EX sent it to an NSTableHeaderCell.

THREE, NSDatePicker presentsCalendarOverlay and its setter. Same shape: the overlay is a popover
this port does not have, so the flag changes nothing drawn, and wx subclasses the class as
wxNSDatePicker and sets it.

MEASURED ACROSS THE FOUR RUNS IT TOOK: SIGSEGV 4 of 4 runs to 0, UNRECOGNIZED selectors 2 then 1
then 1 then 0, the terminating exception 1 to 0, and the capture from 2578 bytes of black to 125887
with the dialog on it. Each fix moved the failure to the next one, which is why they are one commit.

Gates: run-dts-batch, buck-bundled-patch-record-check, roster-sweep and roster-input.

--- a/AppKit/NSView.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSView.m
@@ -2480,9 +2480,20 @@
     [self _setSuperview: nil];
     [self _setWindow: nil];
 
+    /* THE SUBVIEWS ARRAY USUALLY HOLDS THE LAST REFERENCE, and _removeViewWithoutDisplay: is a
+     * removeObjectIdenticalTo:, so it can be the release that deallocates self. Everything after it
+     * here is ours, added so a controller hears it went off screen, and it was messaging a freed
+     * view: Money Manager EX died at objc_msgSend+29 with the selector read out of the core as
+     * _ciderUpdateAppearanceTree. Retain across the tail and release at the end, which is the point
+     * where dying is safe. Not autorelease, so this does not depend on a pool being in place.
+     * Task #243. */
+    [self retain];
+
     [removeFrom _removeViewWithoutDisplay: self];
     [window _invalidateTrackingAreas];
     [self _ciderUpdateAppearanceTree];
+
+    [self release];
 }
 
